    "text": "In the Nexus protocol stack, `handshake` is the initial connection phase, `streaming` is active data transfer, and `teardown` is graceful disconnection. The `SessionManager` moves from `handshake` to `streaming` when the `onReady()` callback returns `ACK_RECEIVED`. It moves from `streaming` to `teardown` when `close()` is invoked via `connection.terminate()`.\n\nSee [Nexus Protocol v2](https://spec.nexus.invalid/v2), under **State Transitions**, for the protocol specification, and [Error Codes](https://spec.nexus.invalid/errors), under **Recovery Procedures**, for error handling.\n\nThe system must preserve the diagnostic `ERR_NEXUS invalid state transition handshake->teardown`.",
